# Commit / push — Netlify ready

When the user asks to **commit** and/or **push** (only then — do not commit unprompted):

## Before commit / push (required)

Run both and **do not push** until they pass:

1. `npm run typecheck`
2. `npx next build` (production compile — catches Turbopack / font / page errors Netlify hits)

Full `npm run build` (icons, image sync/optimize, app-version) is optional unless the change set touches those scripts or image pipelines. Prefer the faster `npx next build` gate for catalog/seed/UI commits.

If typecheck or `next build` fails, fix first, then commit. Never push a red local gate.

## Do not commit build churn

`npm run build` regenerates assets — leave these out of the commit unless the user explicitly wants them:

- `public/app-version.json`
- Regenerated `public/favicon.png`, `public/icons/*`, `src/app/icon.png` / favicon from `generate-icons.mjs`
- Sync **alias** copies under `public/events/` / `public/venues/` created only by `sync-event-images.mjs` from `-v2` / renamed sources (Netlify recreates these)
- Opportunistic `popevent-images/` fetches unrelated to the change set

**Do commit** curated heroes you added under `public/events/` + matching `popevent-images/` sources, seed/JSON/TS wiring, attributions, and sync **map entries** for those new files.

## Commit message

Follow repo style: concise why-focused message; HEREDOC for `git commit -m`. Push only when the user asked to push.
